<title>USA: Norfolk Southern Q4 oper income rises.</title>
<headline>Norfolk Southern Q4 oper income rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>FOURTH QUARTER			   1996	   1995</p>
<p> Total Transportation Oper Revs $1,179.9    $1,155.2</p>
<p>Total Transportation</p>
<p>   Operating Expenses		  870.1	 900.2</p>
<p> Income from Operations		309.8	 255.0</p>
<p> Nonoperating Income (Expense)	 0.5	   5.0</p>
<p> Net Income			   $  200.5    $  176.9</p>
<p> EPS				    $   1.60    $   1.37</p>
<p> Railway Operating Ratio (%)	  70.5	  75.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Fourth-quarter results in 1995 include costs of an early retirement program, which reduced net income $20.4 million, or 16 cents per share.</p>
<p>Excluding the charge, 1995 fourth quarter net income was $197.3 million; EPS $1.53; and Railway Operating Ratio, 71.6.  </p>
<p>     YEAR				  1996	   1995</p>
<p>Total Transportation</p>
<p>	Operating Revenues	    $4,770.0    $4,668.0</p>
<p>Total Transportation</p>
<p>	Operating Expenses	     3,573.0     3,581.7</p>
<p>Income from</p>
<p>	Operations			 1,197.0     1,086.3</p>
<p>Nonoperating</p>
<p>	Income (Expense)		    (0.1)	 28.4</p>
<p>    Net Income			  $  770.4    $  712.7</p>
<p>    Earnings Per Share		$   6.09    $   5.44</p>
<p>Railway Operating</p>
<p>	Ratio (%)			     71.6	  73.5</p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 year results includes the effect of an accounting charge related to an early retirement program completed in October 1995.</p>
<p>Excluding the charge, for the 1995 year, Net Income was $733.1 million; earnings per share, $5.60; and the Railway Operating Ratio, 72.7.</p>
</text>
